WHY THIS IS NOT AN OPEN LICENCE, STATED RATHER THAN IMPLIED

This is a portfolio artifact. It is published so that it can be READ -- the
design, the boundary between reads and writes, the gates on every write, and
the audit trail of what was measured and what was refused. It is not published
so that it can be run.

The reason is specific to what it does. This server drives an authenticated
LinkedIn session, and LinkedIn's User Agreement restricts automated access to
the site. A permissive licence would invite strangers to point it at their own
accounts, or at other people's, with the author's name on the repository that
showed them how. Reading it carries none of that risk; running it carries all
of it, and the person who would bear the consequence is not the author.

If you want to do something with this beyond reading it, ask first.

